    {
      "id": "case-errorpath-ruc-post-create-failure-direction",
      "behaviors": [
        "bhv-run-user-commands-hook-failure"
      ],
      "context": [],
      "scenarioContext": {
        "sdim-operation": "run-user-commands",
        "sdim-config-source": "image",
        "sdim-container-state": "running",
        "sdim-features": "none",
        "sdim-layering": "cli-overlay",
        "sdim-output-mode": "human"
      },
      "inputClass": "malformed",
      "errorPathTier": true,
      "oracleType": "spec-expectation",
      "resourceGroup": "docker-shared",
      "operations": [
        {
          "id": "op-up",
          "subcommand": "up",
          "argv": [
            "--workspace-folder",
            "${WORKSPACE}"
          ],
          "fixtures": [
            "fx-ruc-hook-failure"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "op-ruc",
          "subcommand": "run-user-commands",
          "argv": [
            "--workspace-folder",
            "${WORKSPACE}",
            "--override-config",
            "${WORKSPACE}/.devcontainer/failing.json"
          ],
          "expectFailurePhase": "lifecycle:postCreate"
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "channel": "chan-exit-code",
          "operation": "op-up",
          "assertion": {
            "equals": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "channel": "chan-exit-code",
          "operation": "op-ruc",
          "assertion": {
            "nonZero": true
          }
        }
      ],
      "cleanup": {
        "containers": true,
        "images": false,
        "networks": true,
        "volumes": true,
        "tempdir": true
      },
      "notes": "Pins the direction of the divergence characterized by `wvr-ruc-completed-hooks-not-rerun` for `postCreateCommand`, the hook whose differential (`case-run-user-commands-hook-failure`) was authored in 024 US3 believing the reference agreed. Direction-pinning twin (FR-043, the 023 T074 lesson). Its differential sibling proves only that the two CLIs disagree, and would stay green if BOTH started reporting success — at which point the record that was supposed to say which side is right would say nothing. This case asserts deacon's side outright: the run FAILS. That is the side the specification's account of lifecycle commands supports (a command that exits non-zero has not completed the container's setup) and the side that keeps `run-user-commands` usable as an explicit re-run, its `--skip-post-create` / `--skip-post-attach` / `--skip-non-blocking-commands` flags being the opt-out. The preceding `up` is asserted to SUCCEED, so a failure here can only come from the hook rather than from a container that never came up."
    },
    {
