      "notes": "Error-path tier, lifecycle stage, at `updateContentCommand` — the hook BEFORE `postCreateCommand`, so the case pins that a mid-sequence failure stops the sequence rather than being carried past. The preceding `up` succeeds on a configuration with no hooks at all, so both sides reach the lifecycle stage from a clean container and the failing hooks arrive as a command-line overlay. The two sides then disagree: deacon runs the overlay's hooks and exits non-zero; the reference skips every hook the container has already completed and exits 0 having executed nothing. Tolerated on `chan-exit-code.exitCode` under `wvr-ruc-completed-hooks-not-rerun`; the DIRECTION is pinned by the spec-expectation twin `case-errorpath-ruc-update-content-failure-direction`, because a differential alone stays green if both sides start reporting success."
