          "channel": "chan-stdout",
          "operation": "op-read-hooks",
          "assertion": {
            "matches": "config-onCreate[\\s\\S]*config-updateContent[\\s\\S]*config-postCreate[\\s\\S]*config-postStart"
          }
        }
      ],
      "cleanup": {
        "containers": true,
        "images": false,
        "networks": true,
        "volumes": true,
        "tempdir": true
      },
      "notes": "FR-037, the ordering half. Each hook appends its own name to a file inside the container, so the file IS the observed order — `onCreate`, then `updateContent`, then `postCreate`, then `postStart`. An exit code cannot distinguish 'ran in order' from 'ran at all', and the Feature-contributed `postCreateCommand` is asserted by its own sibling case so a failure names which of the two facts broke."
    },
